Ladybird finds the word to select in the text that flows through inline
elements, stopping at boxes and line breaks. The other engines also read
words across inline elements: Blink’s SelectionController::
SelectClosestWordFromHitTestResult() selects between the flat-tree
positions StartOfWordPosition() and EndOfWordPosition() give, WebKit’s
startOfWord() and endOfWord() walk visible positions across nodes, and
Gecko’s nsIFrame::PeekOffsetForWord() moves on across sibling frames.
